Count the zone registrations so the one that does not return is known

The panel shows the last token at subsystem 7 (ZALLOC), rank LAST, and the table
holds exactly 644 entries pointing at __zone_site_register in that slot.  That
function does one thing -- vm_tag_alloc(site) -- so the stall is inside one of
those 644 calls.

Print every 32nd call with the low bits of its site pointer.  The site pointer is
unique per entry, so the last line names the exact row even when the symbol
table has no name for it, and the count says how far into the batch it got.
---
diff --git a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
--- a/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
+++ b/osfmk/kern/zalloc.c
@@ -2301,4 +2301,9 @@ __zone_site_register(vm_allocation_site_t *site)
 {
+	static uint32_t nio_zreg;
+	uint32_t nio_z = nio_zreg++;
+	if ((nio_z & 7u) == 0u) {
+		printf("\nZ%u:%llx", nio_z, (unsigned long long)(uintptr_t)site & 0xfffffffu);
+	}
 	if (zone_tagging_on) {
 		vm_tag_alloc(site);
 	}

